  "verbalization": "Latrunculin A appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step mechanism involving the targeting of SNU-387, a compound that is a target of multiple substances, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Licochalcone D. These compounds, in turn, are known to interact with prostate cells, suggesting a potential pathway by which Latrunculin A may influence prostate cell function. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, all of which point to SNU-387 as a critical intermediate in the interaction between Latrunculin A and prostate cells. The shared targeting of SNU-387 by different compounds implies a broader role for this molecule in the biological response to Latrunculin A. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a potential mediator in the observed effects, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
